  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: aom\n  version: \"3.15.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://storage.googleapis.com/aom-releases/libaom-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: ea08c38ecc078bc85bb1b691020e52b06250f1a81fe7ca5b624629225081af96\n  patches:\n    # Ship libaom as a shared library only. The aom_static target is still built\n    # (the aom_av1_rc helper links libaom's internal, non-exported symbols from\n    # it) but is renamed and excluded from `install`, so no static archive is\n    # shipped; the shared library's import library keeps the name \"aom\" on Windows.\n    - 0001-Do-not-install-the-static-aom-library.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - cmake\n    - perl\n    - nasm\n    - if: unix\n      then: make\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('aom', upper_bound='x.x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - if: build_platform == target_platform\n        then:\n          - aomenc --help\n          - aomdec --help\n      - if: unix\n        then:\n          - test -f ${PREFIX}/include/aom/aom.h\n          - test -f ${PREFIX}/lib/libaom${SHLIB_EXT}\n          - test ! -f ${PREFIX}/lib/libaom.a\n          - test -f ${PREFIX}/lib/pkgconfig/aom.pc\n      - if: win\n        then:\n          - if not exist %LIBRARY_INC%\\\\aom\\\\aom.h exit 1\n          - if not exist %LIBRARY_BIN%\\\\aom.dll exit 1\nabout:\n  license: BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Alliance for Open Media video codec\n  description: |\n    AOMedia Video 1 (AV1), is an open, royalty-free video coding format designed for\n    video transmissions over the Internet.\n  homepage: https://aomedia.org/\n  repository: https://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - matthiasdiener\n    - \"0xbe7a\"\n",
